# The Linux personality, in a domain of its own -- RFC 0032 step 3, and the
# first time RFC 0005's "a service domain, not the nucleus" has been true of
# anything.
#
# One endpoint, and nothing else -- not even a console. That is the whole of
# its authority, and it is what makes the containment claim checkable rather
# than asserted: a bug in the largest untrusted-input parser this project will
# ever have reaches one endpoint. When it grows a hosted process's files and
# sockets it will hold *those*, and a reviewer will see them on this list.
package linuxd
version 0.1.0

program bin/linuxd
entry hertz
cap serve linux

payload bin/linuxd from user/linuxd/target/x86_64-unknown-none/release/linuxd
